            "The employee whose mood visibly lifts after being publicly recognized, and who seems to fish for credit, is often running high on a need for significance",
            "The employee who seems to care more about team lunches and inside jokes than almost anything else is often running high on a need for connection",
            "The employee who asks the most questions about \"what's next for me here\" is often running high on a need for growth",
